# USE WHEN implementing message commands, understanding command examples, or troubleshooting command usage

# Message Command Examples

## Overview

This reference document provides comprehensive examples of message-commands used in the 1000xbrain cognitive architecture, organized by mode and purpose. These examples demonstrate proper syntax and usage patterns for various workflow types.

## Basic Message-Command Structure

All message-commands follow this general format:

```
message-command: standard-parameter @project-rule-parameter.mdc
```

Where:
- `message-command:` is the actual command (e.g., `plan-mode:`)
- `standard-parameter` is an optional parameter that modifies the command (e.g., `rules-workflow`)
- `@project-rule-parameter.mdc` is an optional parameter that provides detailed execution instructions

## Planning Mode Examples

### Template Creation

```
# Generate requirements content with basic template
create-template: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-basic.mdc

# Generate detailed requirements content with advanced template
create-template: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-advanced.mdc

# Handle template hallucination issues
create-template: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/helpers/analysis/template-hallucination.mdc
```

### Planning Initialization

```
# Basic planning with rules workflow
plan-mode: rules-workflow

# Subsystem enhancement planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/subsystem-enhancement.mdc

# Error recovery planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/error-recovery.mdc

# Performance optimization planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/performance-optimization.mdc

# System-wide enhancement planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/system-wide-enhancement.mdc

# Basic template with planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-basic.mdc

# Advanced template with planning
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-advanced.mdc

# Advanced template with performance optimization
plan-mode: rules-workflow @parameters/rules/plan-mode/performance-optimization.mdc @parameters/rules/plan-mode/template-advanced.mdc
```

### Planning Continuation and Verification

```
# Continue planning process after initial work
continue-planning: @parameters/rules/plan-mode/continue-planning.mdc

# Verify planning completeness
verify-planning: @parameters/rules/helpers/verification/verify-planning.mdc

# Signal planning completion
planning-document-complete
```

